CAT = "cpaiscFrameworks"; SEG = "FRM"
Q = [
("Which of these is a covered entity under HIPAA?",
 "Health care clearinghouse", ["Life insurance company", "Employer sponsoring a health plan", "Workers' compensation carrier"],
 "HIPAA covers health plans, health care clearinghouses and providers who transmit health information electronically in standard transactions. Life insurance and workers' compensation are excluded from the health plan definition, and an employer is not covered just by sponsoring a plan."),
("The HIPAA minimum necessary standard does not apply to disclosures:",
 "To a provider for treatment", ["To a business associate", "For payment purposes", "For health care operations"],
 "45 CFR 164.502(b) exempts disclosures to or requests by a health care provider for treatment. Payment, operations and disclosures to business associates must still be limited to the minimum necessary."),
("Under HIPAA, an impermissible disclosure of protected health information is presumed to be a breach unless:",
 "It shows low probability of compromise", ["Fewer than 500 individuals are affected", "The information stayed inside the entity", "Individuals are told within 60 days"],
 "Section 164.402 presumes a breach unless the entity shows a low probability that the information was compromised, based on at least four factors. The 500 figure decides media and HHS notice, not whether a breach occurred."),
("A breach of unsecured protected health information affects more than 500 residents of one state. Besides the individuals, the covered entity must notify:",
 "Prominent media in that state", ["The attorney general of that state", "Every other covered entity", "The national consumer credit bureaus"],
 "Section 164.406 requires notice to prominent media outlets serving the state for a breach involving more than 500 of its residents, in addition to individual notice and notice to the Secretary of HHS."),
("Under the HIPAA Security Rule, a security incident includes any:",
 "Attempted unauthorized access", ["Confirmed disclosure of PHI", "Breach affecting 500 or more", "Attack by an outside party"],
 "Section 164.304 defines a security incident as an attempted or successful unauthorized access, use, disclosure, modification or destruction of information, or interference with system operations. Attempts count."),
("Which of these is one of the six principles for processing personal data in GDPR Article 5(1)?",
 "Data minimisation", ["Data portability", "Right to erasure", "Data protection by design"],
 "Article 5(1) lists lawfulness, fairness and transparency; purpose limitation; data minimisation; accuracy; storage limitation; and integrity and confidentiality. Portability and erasure are rights, and protection by design is Article 25."),
("Under GDPR Article 33, a controller must notify the supervisory authority of a personal data breach, where feasible, within:",
 "72 hours of becoming aware", ["24 hours of becoming aware", "30 days of becoming aware", "60 days of becoming aware"],
 "Article 33(1) sets 72 hours after the controller becomes aware, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk to people's rights and freedoms. A later notice must give reasons for the delay."),
("Under GDPR Article 33, when a processor becomes aware of a personal data breach, it must:",
 "Notify the controller without undue delay", ["Notify the data subjects directly", "Notify the supervisory authority in 72 hours", "Notify anyone only if risk is high"],
 "Article 33(2) requires the processor to notify the controller without undue delay. The controller then decides on notice to the supervisory authority and the data subjects."),
("Replacing customer names with codes, while keeping the table that links codes to names separately, is what GDPR calls:",
 "Pseudonymisation", ["Anonymisation", "Data masking", "Data minimisation"],
 "Article 4(5) defines pseudonymisation as processing so data can no longer be attributed to a person without additional information kept separately. Data that can be relinked is still personal data, unlike anonymous data."),
("Under GDPR Article 12, a controller must respond to a data subject's request to exercise a right within:",
 "One month of receipt", ["72 hours of receipt", "45 days of receipt", "90 days of receipt"],
 "Article 12(3) requires action without undue delay and within one month, extendable by two further months for complex or numerous requests. The 72 hours applies to breach notice to the authority."),
("Under GDPR Article 6, an employer processing an employee's bank details to pay salary relies most directly on which lawful basis?",
 "Performance of a contract", ["Consent of the employee", "Controller's legitimate interests", "Vital interests"],
 "Paying wages is necessary to perform the employment contract, which is Article 6(1)(b). Consent is a weak basis in employment because it must be freely given and can be withdrawn."),
("Under PCI DSS, which data element may never be stored after a card authorization, even if encrypted?",
 "Card verification code", ["Primary account number (PAN)", "Cardholder name", "Expiration date"],
 "Card verification codes are sensitive authentication data, which must not be stored after authorization even if encrypted. The PAN may be stored if it is rendered unreadable."),
("PCI DSS Requirement 10, log and monitor all access to system components and cardholder data, falls under which goal?",
 "Regularly monitor and test networks", ["Implement strong access control measures", "Maintain a vulnerability management program", "Maintain an information security policy"],
 "PCI DSS groups Requirements 10 and 11 under regularly monitor and test networks. Requirements 7 to 9 make up the strong access control goal."),
("Which function did NIST CSF 2.0 add to the five functions of the earlier version?",
 "Govern", ["Identify", "Recover", "Monitor"],
 "CSF 2.0, published in February 2024, added Govern to Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond and Recover. Monitor is not a CSF function."),
("Under NIST CSF 2.0, comparing a Current Profile with a Target Profile helps an organization:",
 "Find gaps and plan actions", ["Choose its Tier level", "Certify its CSF compliance level", "Rank the six Functions"],
 "The CSF suggests a gap analysis between Current and Target Profiles followed by a prioritized action plan. The CSF is voluntary and offers no certification."),
("Under NIST CSF 2.0, which Tier describes cybersecurity risk management done ad hoc, case by case?",
 "Tier 1, Partial", ["Tier 2, Risk Informed", "Tier 3, Repeatable", "Tier 4, Adaptive"],
 "Tier 1 is Partial: an ad hoc approach with limited awareness of cybersecurity risk. The Tiers progress to Adaptive, with continuous improvement."),
("The NIST Privacy Framework is made up of which three parts?",
 "Core, Profiles, Implementation Tiers", ["Functions, Categories, Subcategories", "Notice, Choice, Consent, Access", "Govern, Control, Communicate"],
 "Like the Cybersecurity Framework, the Privacy Framework has a Core, Profiles and Implementation Tiers. Functions, Categories and Subcategories are the levels within the Core."),
("NIST SP 800-53 Revision 5 organizes its security and privacy controls into how many families?",
 "20", ["17", "18", "12"],
 "SP 800-53 Rev. 5 lists 20 control families, 17 of which align with the FIPS 200 minimum security requirements. The CIS Controls number 18 and PCI DSS has 12 requirements.",
 20),
("CIS Control 1 in CIS Controls v8.1 covers:",
 "Inventory of enterprise assets", ["Data protection and recovery", "Account management", "Secure configuration of assets"],
 "CIS Control 1 is Inventory and Control of Enterprise Assets, because an organization cannot protect devices it does not know about. Data protection is Control 3."),
("Which of these is one of the seven components of a governance system in COBIT 2019?",
 "Culture, ethics and behavior", ["Design factors", "Capability levels", "Focus areas"],
 "COBIT 2019's components are processes; organizational structures; information flows; people, skills and competencies; culture, ethics and behavior; policies and procedures; and services, infrastructure and applications. Design factors and focus areas shape the system but are not components."),
]
